    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm studying phonetics and i'm a bit confused. can you explain the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives? specifically the difference between /s/ and /z/ sounds in terms of what the vocal cords are doing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The difference between /s/ and /z/ lies in vocal cord vibration, which determines whether the sound is voiced or unvoiced. For the unvoiced alveolar fricative /s/, your vocal cords remain open and do not vibrate while air is forced through the narrow opening. In contrast, the voiced alveolar fricative /z/ involves the vocal cords vibrating as air escapes through the same constricted place of articulation.",
